ds ('the first branch-wide review'), so it is a stated consequence and not a defect. It is noted so the boundary review can weigh it. No edit is wanted in this delta.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261123T142904Z-0bd6c78e", "fid": "R-1"}, "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "owner-rulings.md's transcription note still describes the superseded predicate", "recommendation": "`.prawduct/owner-rulings.md` lines 414-415 say 'The implementation follows the approved words: ... the first whole-plan review that names no new chunk'. That is the predicate this delta replaced with 'the first `cumulative`'. This is a record gap and the fixes are still uncommitted, so it rides that commit. Make the clause relational to the code, or state the new predicate there. Do not edit the owner's quoted words.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261123T142904Z-0bd6c78e", "fid": "R-3"}, "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "Review-history ids moved from the docstring into test docstrings", "recommendation": "The fix deleted 'R-9(a)' from `_cadence_round_ids`. The new test docstrings add 'Renegotiated in round 4 (R-1, R-3, native)' and 'Round 4 (R-2): ...'. Apply the same deletion there if a commit touches them anyway. The behavioural sentences stand without the ids. Nothing reads them.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261123T142904Z-0bd6c78e", "fid": "O-7"}, "oid": "O-3"}], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `fix/round-budget-cadence`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunks_declared": false, "chunks_evidence": {}, "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/changes/round-budget-cadence.md", "plugin/docs/project-state-keys.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null